# Defaults for running the GitHub Actions workflows locally with `act` (https://nektosact.com).
# Prefer `make act-<job>` (e.g. `make act-test`, `make act-build`, `make act-smoke`): it scopes act to ci.yml — every
# workflow has a job called `build`, so a bare `act -j build` runs three of them. The container job
# resolves Conan dependencies from the network (act cannot add a cache mount to a job that declares its
# own container `options`). Steps that need GitHub services (OIDC, artifacts API, code scanning)
# are guarded with `if: ${{ !env.ACT }}` (steps) or `github.actor != 'nektos/act'` (jobs).
#
# The toolchain image must be present locally under the name the workflows use:
#   docker pull ghcr.io/andrewczwu/fileops-cpp-build:main     (or: make build-image BUILD_IMAGE=ghcr.io/andrewczwu/fileops-cpp-build:main)
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04
--container-architecture linux/amd64
--action-offline-mode
--pull=false
--artifact-server-path /tmp/act-artifacts
